{
  // Four agents read the same codebase from different angles, one merges them.
  // Read-only: every agent runs in `plan` permission mode.
  "version": 1,
  "name": "research-fanout",
  "description": "Understand an unfamiliar codebase from four angles at once",
  "concurrency": 4,
  "permissionMode": "plan",
  "maxTurns": 20,
  "vars": {
    "question": "How does this project handle configuration and where does it come from?"
  },
  "agents": [
    {
      "id": "entrypoints",
      "role": "entry points",
      "prompt": "Question:\n\n{{vars.question}}\n\nAnswer it by tracing the entry points: binaries, main functions, CLI wiring. Cite file:line. Do not modify anything."
    },
    {
      "id": "dataflow",
      "role": "data flow",
      "prompt": "Question:\n\n{{vars.question}}\n\nAnswer it by following the data: which structures carry it, where it is read and written. Cite file:line. Do not modify anything."
    },
    {
      "id": "tests",
      "role": "tests",
      "prompt": "Question:\n\n{{vars.question}}\n\nAnswer it from the tests: what the suite asserts about this area tells you what the intended behaviour is. Cite file:line. Do not modify anything."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs",
      "role": "docs and history",
      "prompt": "Question:\n\n{{vars.question}}\n\nAnswer it from documentation, comments and git history. Note anywhere the docs and the code disagree. Do not modify anything."
    },
    {
      "id": "synthesis",
      "role": "synthesiser",
      "dependsOn": ["entrypoints", "dataflow", "tests", "docs"],
      "outputKey": "answer",
      "prompt": "Question:\n\n{{vars.question}}\n\nFour agents investigated in parallel.\n\n--- entry points ---\n{{outputs.entrypoints}}\n\n--- data flow ---\n{{outputs.dataflow}}\n\n--- tests ---\n{{outputs.tests}}\n\n--- docs and history ---\n{{outputs.docs}}\n\nWrite one answer. Where they contradict each other, check the code yourself and say which is right. Drop anything none of them supported with a file reference."
    }
  ]
}
